  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 142 PM CDT Sat Apr 18 2026\n\nA shortwave trough slides across the Desert Southwest and over our\nregion Sunday into Monday, providing below normal temperatures \nand low to medium (10-40%) rain chances areawide. Cloud coverage \nwill help keep temperatures in the 60s across the Permian Basin \nand the Lower Trans Pecos, while the western portions of our \nregion top out in the 70s Monday. Temperatures warm up Tuesday \nand Wednesday as upper ridging briefly builds back in. Highs \nrange in the 70s and 80s Tuesday, then in the 80s and 90s \nWednesday. Wednesday afternoon through Thursday, an upper trough \nswings over the western CONUS, reaching New Mexico by Thursday \nmorning. The approaching trough leads to increased westerly and \nsouthwesterly winds aloft. The associated lee trough allows for \nbreezy south/southwest winds and dry conditions. Strongest winds \nwould likely be found within the Guadalupe/Delaware mountains. \nDownslope winds push highs in the mid 80s to 90s Thursday. This \nmay also be a day to monitor for the potential of fire weather \nconditions, especially over southeast New Mexico. A cold front \nlooks to drop down sometime Friday, sending temperatures into a \ncooling trend for the upcoming weekend.",
